{"operations":[{"content":"def median(data):\n    \"\"\"Return the median of the data as a float.\n\n    For an even number of values, the median is the arithmetic mean of the two middle values.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        raise ValueError(\"median() arg is an empty sequence\")\n    sorted_data = sorted(data)\n    n = len(sorted_data)\n    mid = n // 2\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return float(sorted_data[mid])\n    else:\n        return (sorted_data[mid - 1] + sorted_data[mid]) / 2.0\n","expected_sha256":"5e709a9023ba164147b4ab70d268e25b7f2f77921b22213a59b2bf5c610fbaf2","kind":"modify","path":"src/stats.py"}],"rationale":"Fixed median function to correctly compute the arithmetic mean of the two middle values for even-length data as a float, preserving the public API and existing tests."}